# Mobile factory

- Icerde **writes** mobile apps; it is not one.
- Pipeline: brief → user-selected stack → agent writes frontend + backend + Maestro YAML → files on disk.
- Do not hard-code a single mobile stack as the only option. First implementation may ship one adapter; the interface must allow others.
- OpenCode is the writer. The agent runs in the background.
- The person only writes in **Icerde chat**. Never launch the OpenCode TUI. GraphQL `sendProjectMessage` → headless `opencode run --dir --auto` (`--continue` on follow-ups).
- The **customer does not install OpenCode**. Icerde’s installer vendors the CLI into `vendor/bin`. PATH / `ICERDE_OPENCODE_BIN` is a developer fallback only.
- Output layout: `frontend/`, `backend/`, `maestro/`, `README`.
- Zip/git handoff is that tree in the **selected language** (Expo TypeScript, Flutter Dart, native Swift/Kotlin). `preview/` HTML is a studio mock and is **not** in the zip.
- Backend files target a user-chosen provider when Connections exist (local default today). Never upload the generated app to Icerde hosting. Read [docs/mobile-factory.md](docs/mobile-factory.md) and [docs/connections.md](docs/connections.md).
